      <h2 class="section-title">A gym built by coaches, not investors.</h2>
      <p>IronFit opened its doors in 2013, when two career coaches — <em>Marcus Cole and Elena Voss</em> — got tired of watching people pay for gym memberships they never used. They leased a derelict warehouse on Foundry Street, spent six months welding rigs and painting walls, and built the gym they'd always wanted to train in.</p>
      <p>Twelve years and one extension later, the mission hasn't changed: coaching first, equipment second, sales tactics never. Nobody here will promise you a six-week transformation. What we promise is a plan, a coach who knows your name, and a floor full of people who notice when you don't show up.</p>
